WEBVTT

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.180
It's so heavy.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:48.220
Looks like we bought too much in the end.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.810
Thanks to Maki who just kept stuffing everything into the basket.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.010
Don't mind it!

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.570
Ouch...

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.910
Are you all right, Maki?

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.220
I lost my balance.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.840
Are you hurt?

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:08.400
I'm okay.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.470
The eggs are all broken.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:13.450
Sorry.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:16.780
It's okay, we can always buy them again later.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.400
I'll pay you back some other time.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.720
It's all right.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.740
Speaking of which, that wind was quite strong.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.710
Perhaps it's the first breeze of Spring.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:25.960
Did it only blow for Haruka?

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:29.920
That was lame.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.940
Pay me back for the eggs, okay?

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.650
Uh... I'm sorry.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.000
People find that kind of stuff really funny!

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.360
I know, I know!

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.460
Just thinking about it makes me laugh.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.010
Is that so?

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.140
What program do you usually watch, Atsuko?

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.690
I...

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.430
This girl only watches the news.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.150
What? How can you be so serious?

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.990
Besides, what's so interesting about watching the news?

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:10.680
She finds it interesting to learn about different things related to our society.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:14.270
Things related to society would mean cases and accidents, right?

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:15.480
N–No...

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.430
Things like current events and sports.

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.070
I need to go to the bathroom for a bit.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.820
Okay! Come back quickly and tell us all about the fascinating and interesting news.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:25.930
Okay...

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:27.360
Huh?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.310
Ah, he came.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.770
You guys bought a cat?

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.330
No, we didn't. It comes here once in a while.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:39.220
This is the fourth floor though. How did it climb up onto the veranda?

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.600
Maybe it used the elevator?

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:41.250
No way!

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.310
Yeah, I lied.

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:45.420
I suppose you did.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:48.160
You sure used the bathroom quickly, Atsuko.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.390
What the? Are you playing some kind of game?

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:54.140
Play? What do you mean?

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:55.610
What, you ask...

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.320
Hey, it's going under the kotatsu.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.060
What's wrong?

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.580
I think I left my handkerchief in there.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:09.660
It came out.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:15.700
Atsuko is so... so adorable.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.140
Is that guy the reincarnation of Atsuko?

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.330
She isn't dead yet.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.240
That's my mandarin orange!

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:26.020
Don't be so stingy!

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:33.680
Atsuko.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:34.770
You called?

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.030
W–What?

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:47.890
The reason I gathered everyone here today is to make an important announcement.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:48.820
What? What?

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.180
Spring is coming soon.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.210
Spring will soon cause those idiots to become more active.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.760
Who are these idiots you speak of?

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.410
Isn't that you, Kana-chan?

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.500
No, no, it's probably you, Maki-chan.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:10.410
Therefore, in order to respond swiftly to the foolish actions of these idiots, we have to undergo rebuttal training.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:14.710
I wonder what kind of education Chiaki-chan of the Minami household has received.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.230
Now then, please repeat after me.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:19.160
I'm going to start.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.360
O–Okay.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:23.200
There's only 100 million yen.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.570
T–There's only 100 million yen...

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:28.350
When would you use that as a rebuttal?

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:30.970
What the heck, you bastard?

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:33.360
What the heck... you bastard?

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.530
That rebuttal, where are you guys from?

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:38.890
Hey, Maki-chan. This is bad.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:41.450
Those two are starting to practice rebuttals!

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.990
Isn't that a good thing?

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:45.990
You're right! It's a good thing!

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:49.620
No, no, are you all right with this, Maki-chan?

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:55.170
They're practicing rebuttals without you, so that must mean they think you're an idiot.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:55.710
Is that so?

00:05:56.240 --> 00:06:02.800
Yeah, Chiaki clearly separates the idiots and the non-idiots into separate folders.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.540
Isn't there a folder for family members to use?

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:07.720
Only Haruka has a shortcut on her desktop!

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.010
Hey Chiaki, buy me a computer.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.780
I'm busy right now.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:20.270
Putting that aside, Kana-chan. I just looked through the stuff Haruka bought earlier.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.640
Tonight's dinner will probably be grilled fish.

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.450
Meat... I want to eat meat.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:28.610
But didn't you just have sukiyaki before?

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.460
You're right...

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:32.840
Yakiniku. I want to eat yakiniku!

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:36.060
Yakiniku, that's nice.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:37.860
Looks like it's done.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.800
As I thought, it's really delicious!

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.350
Let's see.

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:49.110
Maki-chan. The ribs. The ribs are ready too!

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:53.870
There's also... harami! It won't do without harami!

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.570
Oh, not a bad idea. Hanami.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.100
Flower viewing?

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:02.560
No, no, ha-ra-mi.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.500
Cherry blossoms should still be buds now.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.910
Yeah, that's right. It's harami.

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.190
She's as red as a bud.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:16.860
Like a bud.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:19.930
I'm home.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.160
Welcome back, Haruka!

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:24.730
Listen to this, Chiaki just mistook harami as–

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:26.230
Don't say it, idiot!

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:28.490
Kana, you're going to catch a cold like that.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:30.890
What happened with Chiaki?

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:33.580
Chiaki-chan said she wants to go flower viewing.

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:35.950
Flower viewing?

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:39.730
Rather than flower viewing, it's more like bud viewing.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:40.400
Nice rebuttal...

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:43.240
Sounds interesting.

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:45.070
It's quite cold though, you still want to go?

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:47.780
Haruka-neesama!

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:56.950
I'm so looking forward to it, harami.

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:58.790
Oops, I mean hanami.

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:03.190
This curry is so good.

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:05.890
Since we have the opportunity, let's invite Fuyuki-kun as well.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:10.120
Oh, good idea! I'll go over when I finish eating.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:12.600
Don't cause any trouble for our neighbor, okay?

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:14.350
He won't go.

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:20.690
Hey!

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.990
Fuyuki said he'll go.

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:26.170
All right. Then I'll make preparations for the number of people going.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:29.920
Oh yeah, the bath water is ready. You can go first.

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:31.050
Okay!

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:42.320
Sounds like fun! I want to go! I'll go! I'll go!

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:44.880
But isn't it too early for flower viewing?

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.050
Was it Kana-chan's idea?

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:49.430
Yeah, kind of.

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:51.360
That's just like Kana-chan.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:54.320
Maybe we should tell her straight up that it's too early?

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.350
What're you talking about?

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:57.920
We were just talking about flower viewing.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:00.620
Cherry blossoms still haven't bloomed though.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:02.200
Can you even call that flower viewing?

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.880
I guess not.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:05.440
That sounds so silly.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.740
I'm looking forward to having yakiniku!

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.550
Eh? Aren't we going flower viewing?

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:18.540
Isn't it nice? We can eat yakiniku while viewing flowers.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.960
Yeah, that works too.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:23.030
What are you guys discussing?

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:24.230
Hi, there!

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:25.300
Hi, there...

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:28.980
We were discussing about going flower viewing with everyone.

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:30.240
Flower viewing?

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:31.680
It seems a bit early though.

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:39.450
So there you have it! Come flower viewing with us!

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:41.890
I don't really understand what's going on though...

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.350
But I already have something planned.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.710
What? Is there something more important than flower viewing?

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:48.490
Uhh, I have a practice test...

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:54.900
Y–You can just keep doing your important tests forever and go to sleep!

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.070
Fujioka! Are you free tomorrow?

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:03.720
Tomorrow? Hmm... Tomorrow, I'm free.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:04.910
All right! Then come along.

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:08.840
Okay. Even though I don't know what's happening, I'll come along.

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.430
You're such a good guy.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:13.180
What's with her?

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:20.150
Morning, everyone!

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:23.770
I assume everyone here already knows, the key to flower viewing is getting good spots.

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:25.940
Also, not to mention shopping.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:29.410
That's why, I want to delegate each of you your roles now.

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:31.590
Huh? Where's Makoto?

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:33.280
Now that you mention it, he's probably not coming.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:35.860
What on Earth is that guy doing?

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.500
Didn't he say he would come?

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:41.630
Umm, if you don't mind, I can go pick our spots.

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:42.980
I'll go pick our spots too!

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:45.040
I-I'll go do that too!

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:48.180
But it seems shopping is more interesting after all.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:50.020
I guess I'll go shopping instead.

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:51.190
What should I be doing?

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:53.060
I'm going too.
What should I be doing?

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:55.790
Okay! The three guys can go pick the spots.

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:58.020
Eh? Three?

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:00.660
What are you being so indecisive for?

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.770
Then Uchida, you can help out with the shopping.

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:03.830
All right!

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:04.780
Hey, hey, Kana-chan! Can we buy lots of snacks?

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:07.620
I'll be in your care.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:10.000
Ah, same here.

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:13.220
Then let's all meet up under the cherry tree later.

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:15.140
I wish for everyone's success!

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.700
Yeah!

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.030
All right, are you guys ready?

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:28.840
Roger!

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.290
Let's move out!

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.590
Hey, you two!

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:34.470
They're gone.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.380
They're both so energetic.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.100
That's what I don't like about it.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:46.990
This way is more comfy.

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:48.740
Haruka's home.

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:51.150
It's so peaceful...

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:53.620
I'm about to fall asleep.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:55.990
Hey now, you two.

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:56.960
What is it?

00:11:57.180 --> 00:12:00.240
It's not "What is it?", come help me out.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:03.800
The one who said having grilled meat is too plain was you, Maki.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:06.190
Okay, okay, I'm coming to help you now.

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:07.540
I'm sorry.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:09.010
Here's your apron.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.050
What do you think? Does it suit me?

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:18.980
How could these kinds of clothes suit me?

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:22.410
Well, it can't be helped that Kana wants you to wear that.

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:23.140
Really?

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:26.840
So you just moved in recently?

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:28.040
Yeah.

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:31.050
By the way, what's your relationship with Chiaki-chan?

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:31.560
Eh?

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:34.450
This is full of things that have nothing to do with each other.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:39.860
They're all very cheap! See? I'm unrivaled at shopping.

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:41.240
Put them back.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:43.940
No, there's a chance we might need them.

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:45.530
Canned cat food?

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:48.250
Are you going to eat canned cat food while viewing flowers?

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.880
Hey! Look guys!

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:55.590
Check it out! If we can collect the whole set, we can build a house from it.

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:57.390
Amazing, isn't it?

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:01.660
There's only one part in each box.

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.110
They sure know how to make money.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.570
Cut it out, you two!

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:11.110
Sorry!

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:12.970
Are you all right, Maki?

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:13.880
Did you get hurt?

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:15.310
I'm okay!

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:17.260
Here, use this.

00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:18.470
Thanks.

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:21.540
Oh? Could it be Kana and the others?

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:24.290
Coming!

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:26.410
Yes?

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:26.950
Oh?

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:28.280
Yo!

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:29.500
Hayami-senpai?

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:33.000
You're going flower viewing, aren't you? Count me in.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.180
Here, gifts from me.

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:39.030
How's this area?

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:40.560
Not bad.

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:42.080
The view is good too.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:43.640
There are also trash cans.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:49.770
Yeah... but we should ask for a girl's opinion on these sorts of things.

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:50.920
What do you think, Mako-chan?

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:54.150
Uhh...

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:58.300
It's not bad, right? Probably.

00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:01.270
Really? Then let's use this place.

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:03.610
Us guys don't know much about these things.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.900
Right, Touma?

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:07.880
Yeah... You're right.

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:11.140
Umm, what is it?

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:13.920
You are a girl... right?

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:17.500
Pardon me for asking such a strange question.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:22.890
Do I look like a boy?

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:24.880
I know, right?

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:35.310
Hey, there's still plenty of juice left!

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:42.490
We have to get to where Kana and the others are fast, or the lunchboxes will...

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:45.340
Now, now, it's all good.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:47.160
But...

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:51.580
All right! Next, let's try out this Matatabi Special!

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:03.370
Minami and the others sure are late.

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:04.960
Indeed.

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:08.360
I should've brought my TS along.

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:09.440
Yeah.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:11.460
Hey.

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:14.630
What does TS stand for?

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:16.680
Tandem Screen.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.420
You sure?

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:21.230
Hey! Touma! Fujioka!

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.650
Oh! Over here!

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.920
You're so slow, Kana.

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:31.630
That's not true.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.400
We're the first group here, aren't we?

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:37.330
I don't think you'll see a second group coming here even if you wait all day.

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:43.850
Check this out! You can build a house from this once you've collected all the pieces!

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:45.890
What else did you buy?

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:48.070
Let's see...

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:49.150
This!

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:49.800
Cat food?

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:52.400
By the way, where's Haruka-neesama?

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:54.950
What? They still haven't come?

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:56.600
Maybe they're on their way now.

00:15:56.870 --> 00:16:00.340
Could it be that they've already started eating grilled meat over there?

00:16:00.340 --> 00:16:02.490
No. There's no way that's possible.

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:03.770
I'm going to check on them.

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:04.290
H–Hey!

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:07.710
Minami is so energetic.

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.200
Indeed.

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:15.850
Hey! Haruka!

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:18.300
Everyone's waiting!

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:22.280
Ah! Welcome back, Kana-chan!

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:23.300
What are you guys doing?

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:27.140
You're late, Kana-chan! We've been waiting for you!

00:16:27.890 --> 00:16:30.810
Hurry! Let's drink this together!

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:36.470
Delicious!

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:41.690
Hey Ka-na-chan...

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:42.970
Drink with us?

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:45.860
N–No... Umm...

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:54.730
I have to go to the other side... to discuss what we have to do next... I have to go but... I'll be back.

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:57.370
Eh? All right...

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.050
Here, gifts for you.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.000
I'll take them then.

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:08.310
3!

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:13.720
5!

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.220
Hey!

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:18.060
She's finally back.

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:20.400
Here, gifts.

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:23.690
Huh? Just what were you doing there?

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:25.490
Where's Haruka-neesama?

00:17:25.490 --> 00:17:27.750
Haruka... Well...

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:29.990
I didn't make it in time.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:33.250
I don't understand what you just said.

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:39.400
Well, forget it. I shouldn't have counted on you in the first place. I'll go.

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.370
Take these, Yoshino.

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:43.850
O–Okay.

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.470
Wait for me, Chiaki!

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:47.260
Juice!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.620
Let's drink them.

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:50.650
Eh? What flavors are there?

00:17:56.230 --> 00:17:58.280
The five dangerous faults of a general.

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:00.230
He who is reckless can be killed.

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:02.830
He who is cowardly can be captured.

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:06.010
He who is quick tempered can be insulted.

00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:08.550
He who is moral can be shamed.

00:18:08.550 --> 00:18:11.440
He who is fond of the people can be worried.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:12.240
And finally,

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:13.310
to seize the rider, aim for the horse.

00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:15.960
Isn't he... cold?
to seize the rider, aim for the horse.

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:18.580
Haruka-neesama?

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:21.480
Haruka-neesama, we're about to start flower viewing–

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:25.410
Oh, it's Chiaki-chan!

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:26.430
This is...

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:29.330
This is for you. Cheers!

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:30.920
Thanks.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:39.400
So right there, after that, it's funny, right?!

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:45.280
Like this, facing this way!

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:49.810
This is strange! This is too strange!

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:53.290
Chiaki! Chiaki!

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.760
This is so strange, Chiaki!

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:03.300
Someone please hurry up and come back!

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:24.730
It's coming down harder now.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:29.320
These three minutes must be the longest and most yearning in the world.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:33.110
I even used my own allowance to buy you, you little rascal.

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.820
I'm back!

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:40.330
Damn it! It suddenly started raining.

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:43.160
What? You're completely drenched.

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:46.500
Didn't this morning's forecast say it would rain?

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.590
I didn't bring my umbrella.

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:53.570
Hurry up and change. I'll heat up the bath for you.

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:55.310
Okay.

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:21.220
You're going to die here. You're not someone who's supposed to live.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:25.980
Come, kill me as you wish.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.060
Your ex-fiancée.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.380
Why...

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:36.340
Why did you have to betray the syndicate?

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:37.560
Answer me!

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:41.070
Hey, you can use it in ten minutes...

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:48.230
These noodles...

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:53.190
They're really delicious...

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:05.120
Go use the bath after you finish.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.350
Chiaki? Chiaki?

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:28.890
What is it?

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:31.870
Which flavor do you want?

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:42.710
It's delicious!

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:43.950
It's delicious!

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.340
I'm home!

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:49.570
How come the two of you are eating cup noodles?

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:51.200
It's almost time for dinner, you know.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:52.600
Umm, this is...

00:21:52.600 --> 00:21:55.190
Do you want to try, Haruka? It's really delicious!

00:21:55.190 --> 00:21:56.460
Geez...

00:21:57.060 --> 00:21:59.300
Then I guess I'll have some.

00:21:59.300 --> 00:22:00.770
Yay!

00:23:31.420 --> 00:23:33.820
Have you ever encountered nasal congestion when blowing your nose?

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:36.180
That's because the density of mucus and water are different.

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:38.580
It'll be fine once you rinse it with saltwater.

00:23:38.580 --> 00:23:43.070
Press on the other nostril and breathe in the water through the other, then spit it out from your mouth.

00:23:43.070 --> 00:23:44.010
You'll feel much better then.

00:23:44.010 --> 00:23:45.630
You just have to get to it. Good luck.
